WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.480
Superheroing is a tough business.

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:05.840
One minute you're joking around, punching
bad guys in the face, and the next you're

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:07.419
pushing up fictional daisies.

00:00:07.419 --> 00:00:10.760
Fortunately, when you've got superpowers,
there's a more than decent chance you'll be

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:15.020
resurrected and given new life...usually because
you're more valuable to your parent company

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:16.320
alive than dead.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.780
Will any of these super-people come back to
life in 2018 or beyond?

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:23.250
Probably...but for now, let's pay our respects
and mourn their super-passings.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:26.250
And of course...spoilers ahead.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.160
Logan and Professor X

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:32.040
In a year filled with so many superhero flicks,
it's hard to believe that the R-rated Wolverine

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:35.409
swan song, Logan, actually hit theaters in
2017.

00:00:35.409 --> 00:00:38.390
But it did — and it was basically a superhero
slaughterfest.

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:42.160
In addition to the demise of Caliban, the
D-lister mutant who was played by comedian

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:45.809
Stephen Merchant, Logan gave a final send
off to two characters who've been thrilling

00:00:45.809 --> 00:00:48.350
comic book fans at the movies for nearly 20
years.

00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:52.719
Professor X, played by Sir Patrick Stewart,
met an inglorious end at the hands of an evil

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:56.949
Wolverine clone — but not before he practically
stole the show in the movie that was named

00:00:56.949 --> 00:00:58.510
for a totally different character.

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:02.100
"Two days on the road, only one meal, and
hardly any sleep.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.059
She's 11 and I'm f---ing 90."

00:01:04.059 --> 00:01:07.700
But it was the loss of Logan himself, played
by fan-favorite Hugh Jackman, that fans will

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.509
remember for years to come.

00:01:09.509 --> 00:01:13.560
Jackman's held the role of Wolverine since
2000's original X-Men movie, and his portrayal

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:17.280
is rightly lauded for helping make superhero
movies the force of nature that they've become.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:21.719
Given the chance to take the character out
on his own terms, Jackman helps fans say goodbye

00:01:21.719 --> 00:01:25.829
to Logan at the movie's end in a beautiful
moment that stands out as not just one of

00:01:25.829 --> 00:01:31.850
the most classic moments in a superhero movie,
but one of 2017's best movie moments period.

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:32.850
Patriot

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:36.450
Jeffrey Mace, who in the comics is better
known by his alter ego, the Patriot, debuted

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:39.679
on ABC's Agents of SHIELD in the fall of 2016.

00:01:39.679 --> 00:01:43.399
The character, played by Jason O'Mara, was
revealed to be the new director of the super-spy

00:01:43.399 --> 00:01:47.570
agency, and at first his name felt more like
an Easter Egg — a nod to longtime comics

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:51.630
readers that the show's producers were reaching
far into Marvel's back catalogue for new characters

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:53.840
to play in their small corner of the MCU.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:58.170
As time went on, we learned a whole lot more
about the TV version of Mace: he was supposedly

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:02.369
an Inhuman who used his enhanced strength
and invulnerability for the greater good.

00:02:02.369 --> 00:02:06.789
But as it happened, this was all bogus: Mace
had no powers, and instead took the television

00:02:06.789 --> 00:02:08.720
equivalent of super-steroids.

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:10.540
Sort of like...Crap-tain America.

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:15.920
"No no no no no!"

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:22.500
When the show came back in 2017 after its
mid-season break, Mace and the rest of the

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:26.750
SHIELD team found themselves in the Framework,
a VR simulation where Hydra ran the world,

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:28.110
and the good guys were in hiding.

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:32.170
There, Mace heroically sacrificed himself
to save his fellow agents from doom.

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:36.190
It was a fitting end for the character who,
in the span of only one season, had quickly

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:38.720
became a favorite of fans of the show.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:39.720
Black Widow

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:44.730
In the 2016 Marvel Comics event Civil War
II, an Inhuman who can see the future shares

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.640
a vision with Marvel's heroes.

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:50.900
In it, Miles Morales stands on the steps of
the US Capitol, his costume soaked in blood,

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:53.090
clutching Captain America's lifeless body.

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:55.990
It's a provocative image, and yet it took
a while to get more information.

00:02:55.990 --> 00:02:59.920
Then, all the heroes got pretty busy when
Captain America revealed that he was actually

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:04.170
a Hydra sleeper agent, took over S.H.I.E.L.D.,
and conquered the United States.

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:06.810
Man...talk about a real Crap-tain America.

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:10.840
In the follow-up Marvel Comics event story,
Secret Empire, Miles and Steve Rogers met

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:13.430
face-to-face — but neither of them counted
on Natasha.

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:18.340
While Cap and Spider-Man squared off in Secret
Empire #7, the Black Widow had already been

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:22.400
watching on a nearby roof with a sniper-rifle,
hoping to end Captain America's reign with

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:23.570
a single bullet.

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:26.590
When the fight broke out, Black Widow intervened,
hoping to save Spider-Man.

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:31.670
Unfortunately, Captain America's shield broke
Natasha's neck, and she didn't survive.

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:35.620
Once the story was over and finished, the
Cosmic Cube undid all of evil Cap's shenanigans

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:37.700
— but Black Widow stayed underground.

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:40.290
Her funeral took place in Secret Empire #10.

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:43.730
Of course, since she's played by one of the
biggest movie stars on the planet, the chances

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:46.820
of her staying that way for long are basically
slim-to-none.

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:50.840
The Widow will be back in comics pages soon
— count on it.

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:52.010
The Warriors Three

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:56.720
In Thor: Ragnarok, Thor saves most of the
Asgardians from Hela, goddess of the underworld,

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:59.660
with help from Hulk, Valkyrie, and Loki, to
name a few.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:04.300
He doesn't rescue everyone, however: the Warriors
Three, Thor's rambunctious sidekicks, fight

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.470
on the front lines when Hela attacks.

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:08.170
None of them survive the film.

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:12.340
Their defeats are so quick, in fact, that
Marvel Studios president Kevin Feige actually

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:16.030
had to explain that the Warriors Three needed
to get decimated to show how big a threat

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:17.170
Hela was.

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:21.540
It worked...but Thor's corner of the MCU is
poorer for it.

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:22.540
Martin Stein

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:26.790
Any Legends of Tomorrow fan who was paying
attention knew that Dr. Martin Stein, better

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:29.710
known as Firestorm's older half, was on the
way out.

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:33.410
In October, right before Legends returned
for its third season, Deadline announced that

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:37.290
actor Victor Garber, who plays Stein, would
be leaving the show so he could replace David

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:39.590
Hyde Pierce in Broadway's Hello, Dolly! revival.

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:43.960
Soon after the news broke, Legends started
planting the seeds for Garber's departure.

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:47.560
Stein was working on a way to separate himself
from Jefferson Jackson, the young man with

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:50.590
whom he merges to create the superheroic Firestorm.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:52.780
Too bad Nazis show up to spoil the fun.

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:57.120
In a plotline too complicated to adequately
recap here, Stein is shot and separated from

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:00.690
Firestorm, dying after having saved his friends
in the process.

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:03.250
Hello Dolly...goodbye Doctor Stein.

00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:04.810
Yondu Udonta

00:05:04.810 --> 00:05:09.210
The first Guardians of the Galaxy movie introduced
the world at large to Peter Quill's abductor,

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:13.930
the craggy, drawling Ravager who taught Star-Lord
everything he knows about conniving and swiping

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:17.110
stuff, who's also a wizard with that deadly,
whistling arrow thingie.

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:20.620
Comic book fans, on the other hand, know he
was a core member of the original Guardians

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:21.780
of the Galaxy team.

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:25.780
Yondu got his start in the first appearance
of the team in Marvel Super-Heroes #18 in

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:27.190
1969.

00:05:27.190 --> 00:05:31.841
So his turn to the side of good in Guardians
of the Galaxy Vol. 2 — and his heroic sacrifice

00:05:31.841 --> 00:05:36.360
to save his adopted son Peter — made the
loss all the more memorable by movie's end.

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:39.830
His Ravager funeral just before the film's
credits stands out as one of the most touching

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:42.240
moments we've seen in the MCU yet.

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:45.730
Perhaps most importantly, he managed to make
Mary Poppins cool again.

00:05:45.730 --> 00:05:47.389
"You look like Mary Poppins."

00:05:47.389 --> 00:05:49.360
"Is he cool?"

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:51.280
"Hell yeah he's cool."

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.920
"I'm Mary Poppins, y'all!"

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:58.720
For Disney, Marvel's corporate parent, that's
called vertical integration and corporate

00:05:58.720 --> 00:05:59.720
synergy.

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:01.460
And that's the most heroic act of all.

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:02.590
Thanks for watching!

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:04.450
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:07.310
Plus check out all this other cool stuff we
know you'll love too.

